e30†Android L157:       * cite31†Google Play L158:       * cite32†Wear OS L159:       * cite33†See all L160:     * Devices\nL161:       * cite34†Pixel L162:       * cite35†Google Nest L163:       * cite36†Fitbit L164:       * cite37†Chromebook L165:       * cite38†Googlebook L166:       * cite39†See all L167: \nL168: Learn more:\nL169: \nL170: cite40†Google Ads & Commerce blog cite41†Waze blog L171: \nL172:   * Company news\nL173: ### Company news\nL174: \nL175: See all in Company news\nL176: \nL177:     * Outreach & initiatives\nL178: \nL179:       * cite42†Creating opportunity L180:       * cite15†Safety & security L181:       * cite43†Google.org L182:       * cite44†Public policy L183:       * cite45†Sustainability L184:       * cite16†Health L185:       * cite46†See all L186:     * Leadership\nL187: \nL188:       * cite47†Sundar Pichai, CEO L189:       * cite48†More authors L190:       * cite48†See all L191:     * Inside Google\nL192: \nL193:       * cite49†Around the globe L194:       * cite50†Life at Google L195:       * cite51†See all L196: \nL197: Learn more:\nL198: \nL199: cite52†Google Security blog L200: \nL201:   * cite1†Feed L202: Build with Nano Banana Pro, our Gemini 3 Pro Image model\nL203: \nL204: []\nL205: \nL206: Preferences\nL207: \nL208:   * [Select]\nL209: \nL210: Links\nL211: \nL212:   * cite53†Images L213:   * cite54†RSS feed L214: # Build with Nano Banana Pro, our Gemini 3 Pro Image model\nL215: \nL216: Here’s how developers can use Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image), a powerful new image generation and editing model with advanced features and creative control.\nL217: \nL218: * * *\nL219: \nL220: Alisa Fortin\nL221: \nL222: Product Manager, Google DeepMind\nL223: \nL224: Naina Raisinghani\nL225: \nL226: Product Manager, Google DeepMind\nL227: \nL228: * * *\nL229: \nL230: cite55†Image: Image with multiple input-output images with the text Build with Nano Banana Pro in the center†storage.googleapis.com L231: Today, we’re releasing cite56†Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image), a higher-fidelity model built on cite57†Gemini 3 Pro for developers to access studio-quality image generation. This follows our release of cite58†Nano Banana†developers.googleblog.com (Gemini 2.5 Flash Image) just a few months ago.\nL232: Since then, we’ve loved seeing the community put its cite59†key features†github.com to work — from character consistency to cite60†photo restoration†x.com , and even using its capabilities to make cite61†local edits†x.com in an infinite canvas.\nL233: This state-of-the-art image generation and editing model is starting to roll out in paid preview to build a new wave of intelligent, multimodal applications with the cite62†Gemini API†ai.google.dev in cite63†Google AI Studio†ai.studio and cite64†Vertex AI†console.cloud.google.com for enterprises.\nL234: This model unlocks high-fidelity images with higher accuracy in text rendering and robust world knowledge, supercharged by the model's ability to use grounding with Google Search to retrieve data based on the user's prompt.\nL235: Gemini 3 Pro Image excels on Text to Image AI benchmarks.\nL236: \nL237: cite65†Image: Gemini 3 Pro Image Text to Image AI benchmark bar chart compared to other leading competitors†storage.googleapis.com L238: We are also expanding the reach of Gemini 3 Pro Image across the developer ecosystem. In cite66†Google Antigravity†antigravity.google — our new agentic development platform — coding agents can now directly leverage these image generation capabilities to generate detailed UI mockups for user review or even new visual assets before implementing in code. Additionally, leading creative platforms are integrating the model, including Adobe and Figma.\nL239: ## High fidelity and controls\nL240: \nL241: If you’re building advanced tools that require precision, Gemini 3 Pro Image gives you control over the physics (lighting, camera, focus, color grading) and composition of the image to ensure professional-quality outputs.\nL242: \nL243: A silhouette lost in a sea of golden bokeh and morning mist.\nL244: \nL245: Prompt: Replace volumetric lighting with bokeh\nL246: cite67†Image: Image showing a side by side of an input image of the silhouette of a man with scattered sun rays and an output image where the same image with more volumetric lighting using AI†storage.googleapis.com L247: With 2K and 4k resolution available, you can ensure outputs meet resolution standards required for professional production. Effortlessly create cohesive advertisements by combining diverse elements such as product images, logos, and references. Achieve consistent resemblance for up to five individuals, integrate six high-fidelity shots, or blend as many as fourteen standard inputs into a single, polished ad.\nL248: Try our cite68†demo app†aistudio.google.com that allows you to pair logos with products to create your own mockup designs.\nL249: Demo app that brings product design to life with reference images. Sequences shortened.\nL250: ## Improved text rendering and localization\nL251: \nL252: Gemini 3 Pro Image offers a significant leap forward from 2.5 Flash Image, transforming abstract image generation into functional assets. It excels in handling logic and language, and delivers state-of-the-art text rendering, producing clear, accurate text integrated in your images.\nL253: \n"
